{"body":{"text":["Reading Knowledge as text takes about a quarter of a second at the command line over the five stores, where it took 0.8 s while every word was a holon (19/49). On the site a brief opens in 60 to 210 ms once the field is fetched, after the brief's read was found entering every brief beneath it, its stop lost behind a placeholder the engine matches by type (19/39). The engine still lets go of what a use gives beyond what its function takes, without a word, which is to be refused, since nothing is to fail silently (19/39). A move reads again what it read before, nothing kept between reads, and most of its passes to the stores are not for what is shown: each read first learns its vocabulary anew, each function used, its type, its inputs and their types, and the kinds of value, about eight rounds before any work. The engine's whole asking each store its whole question first was built and measured slower in the browser, 280 to 370 ms against 85 to 155, and let go (19/73). Still between: `language/text.ts` keeps the earlier form of expressions for its own tests alone."]},"id":"1M82SFSRRFQJ00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}